# Small vector icons are static geometry, rendered in a single batch per icon.
import lib/sections.dl

class:
    patterns:
        UI icon line
    members:
        left as a floating-point number
        top as a floating-point number
        right as a floating-point number
        bottom as a floating-point number

class:
    patterns:
        UI icon drawing
    members:
        lines as a pointer to UI icon line
        count as an integer

icon line {floating-point number:left} {floating-point number:top} to {floating-point number:right} {floating-point number:bottom} means: @intrinsic("construct", UI icon line, left, top, right, bottom)
a UI icon from {an array:lines} means: @intrinsic("construct", UI icon drawing, @intrinsic("cast", a static reference to lines, a pointer to UI icon line), the length of lines)

to get the UI icon named {C string:name}:
    if name = "paste":
        return a UI icon from [icon line 6.0 5.0 to 19.0 5.0, icon line 19.0 5.0 to 19.0 21.0, icon line 19.0 21.0 to 6.0 21.0, icon line 6.0 21.0 to 6.0 5.0, icon line 9.0 3.0 to 16.0 3.0, icon line 16.0 3.0 to 16.0 7.0, icon line 16.0 7.0 to 9.0 7.0, icon line 9.0 7.0 to 9.0 3.0, icon line 9.0 11.0 to 16.0 11.0, icon line 9.0 15.0 to 16.0 15.0]
